<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Kondurcha River</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1391">1391</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh-timur-war">Tokhtamysh–Timur war</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Kondurcha River was fought on 18 June 1391 near the Kondurcha, a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> basin east of modern Samara. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, after a long march across the steppe, defeated the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a>, khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> and his former protégé. It was the first of two great defeats, followed by the Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terek-river">Terek River</a> in 1395, that ruined the Horde.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-kondurcha-river.jpg" alt="Battle of the Kondurcha River" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stuntelaar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timur_Steppe_campaign.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
